  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_113' aria-label=\" Sunny @ Santosh Dharmu Bhosale versus The State of Maharashtra pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('113','2024','2024_11_1440_1447','2024INSC878'); ><font size='4'> <strong>SUNNY @ SANTOSH DHARMU BHOSALE<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF MAHARASHTRA </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 11 S.C.R. 1440</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 878</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010007092024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : BHUSHAN RAMKRISHNA GAVAI<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, K.V. VISWANATHAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether it was the appellant-accused who assaulted the victim-deceased due to which the death of the deceased has occurred; whether the conviction of the appellant under Section 302 IPC, deserves to be altered to one under Part I of Section 304 IPC. Headnotes&dagger; s.302 and s.304 Part-I &ndash; Prosecution case that PW-6 and her husband-victim went to the house of PW-5 &ndash; Appellant-accused came in front of the house of PW-5 and started abusing PW-5 and his wife on account of a loan they had taken &ndash; Victim intervened &ndash; Appellant abused<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 20-11-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 4664/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Case Partly allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('113','2024','2024_11_1440_1447','2024INSC878','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns